course: dictionary
lesson: 2037
title: A word from the sea
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are new, so you have to work them out. Read the words around the new word, because they are its context. «The Mock Turtle's teacher at the school in the sea was an old conger-eel.» The word eel is part of conger-eel, so a conger must be a kind of eel, and the school in the sea tells you it lives in the sea.
explain: Next, check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The conger eel is a real long sea fish that hides in rocks and wrecks.» A conger is a large sea eel with grey or black skin. It lives in rocky places and wrecks, so the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Some words in Alice are jokes. «Drawling, Stretching and Fainting in Coils» sounds like a school subject, but it is a silly copy of Drawing, Sketching and Painting in Oils. When a word seems odd, ask whether it is a real word, a joke, or both.
fact: A conger is a large sea eel with grey or black skin.
fact: Congers live in rocky places and wrecks in the sea, and they can grow longer than a tall man.
fact: Congers hide in holes and come out at night to hunt.
fact: The word conger can also mean the flesh of the eel, which people eat as food.
fact: Congers are fish, not snakes, even though they look a little like snakes.
fact: Congers can bite hard, so keep your hands away from their mouths.
exercise: «The conger eel, the Mock Turtle's drawing master, is a real long sea fish that hides in rocks and wrecks.» What is a conger? | * A large sea eel that hides in rocks and wrecks | A sweet cake served at school | A small bird that sings at dawn | A tall man who swims well
exercise: Congers hide in holes and come out at night to hunt. When do congers come out to hunt? | * At night | At the start of the school day | In the morning sun | At lunchtime
exercise: Congers can bite hard. What should you do if you see one near you? | * Keep your hands away from its mouth | Pat it gently on the head | Pick it up by the tail | Feed it with your fingers
test: «The Mock Turtle's teacher was an old conger-eel.» Which word in this sentence tells you a conger is a kind of eel? | Mock | * conger-eel | teacher | school
test: Congers can grow longer than a tall man. What does this tell you about a conger? | It is very small and light | It lives on land in the trees | * It can be very long | It can fly like a bird
exam: In Carroll's joke, «Drawling, Stretching and Fainting in Coils» is a silly copy of which real school subject? | Reading and Writing | * Drawing, Sketching and Painting in Oils | Maths and Science | Music and Dance
